    "title": "<span class=\"highlight\">React</span> <span class=\"highlight\">JS</span> <span class=\"highlight\">Developer</span>",
    "description": "Emergency University is an established technology company dedicated to improving public safety and emergency preparedness through innovative web-based education and communication solutions. We are looking for an experienced <span class=\"highlight\">ReactJS</span> <span class=\"highlight\">developer</span> to join our team and help evolve our web platform.\n\nThis is a long-term opportunity for someone who enjoys taking ownership of projects, solving technical challenges, and contributing to products that make a real-world impact.\n\n## What You'll Be Doing\n\nYou'll work directly with our leadership team to maintain, improve, and expand our existing website and web applications.\n\nYour responsibilities will include:\n\n* Developing new features using <span class=\"highlight\">ReactJS</span> and JavaScript\n* Maintaining and improving our existing website\n* Enhancing performance, security, and usability\n* Troubleshooting and resolving production issues\n* Recommending modern <span class=\"highlight\">development</span> practices and technologies\n* Supporting testing, deployment, and production releases\n* Working independently while communicating progress and recommendations\n\n## Required Qualifications\n\n* 5+ years of professional web <span class=\"highlight\">development</span> experience\n* Strong expertise with <span class=\"highlight\">ReactJS</span>\n* Advanced JavaScript skills\n* HTML5 and CSS3\n* Experience building and maintaining production websites\n* Excellent communication skills\n* Ability to work independently with minimal supervision\n* Strong problem-solving and debugging abilities\n\n## Preferred Experience\n\nExperience with any of the following is highly desirable:\n\n* Microsoft IIS\n* ASP / ASP.NET\n* SQL Server\n* T-SQL\n* Stored Procedures\n* Windows Server Administration\n* Legacy application modernization\n* API integration\n\n## Nice to Have\n\n* Git or other version control systems\n* Website optimization and security best practices\n* Experience working with Microsoft technology stacks\n* Experience in healthcare, education, emergency management, or public safety applications\n\n## Contract Details\n\n* Remote\n* Independent Contractor\n* 20–40 hours per week\n* Flexible schedule\n* Long-term engagement for the right candidate\n\n## To Apply\n\nPlease include:\n\n1. A brief introduction about yourself.\n2. Links to <span class=\"highlight\">ReactJS</span> projects you've built.\n3. Your experience with SQL Server, ASP.NET, or Microsoft technologies.\n4. Examples of websites or applications you've maintained or modernized.\n5. Your hourly rate.\n6. Your weekly availability.\n\nWe are looking for someone who takes pride in delivering high-quality work, communicates well, and wants to become a long-term member of our <span class=\"highlight\">development</span> team.",
